      "title": "CMake: Add an option to force 64-bit time_t/Y2038 compliance",
      "message": "CMake: Add an option to force 64-bit time_t/Y2038 compliance\n\nNote that libpcap, if used, as well as any other libraries that have\ntime_t or structs containing time_t in their API will need to have\nbeen compiled with the same size time_t also or else things will\nfail. There is a check for libpcap, but there's a good chance that\nthings will fail, so this is still experimental.\n\nPing #21297\n\nAI-Assisted: no\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-06-25T08:47:58.000-04:00",
